      "math_academy_id": "e-15611",
      "problem": "What is the range of the function $f(x) = -4\\cos(3x)-2?$",
      "worked_solution": "The range of $\\cos x$ is\n\n$$\n-1 \\leq \\cos x \\leq 1.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n-1\\leq\\cos\\left(3x \\right) \\leq 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-4$ and then subtracting $2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\le 1 \\\\ 4 & \\ge -4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\ge -4 \\\\ 2 & \\ge -4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-2\\ge -6 \\\\ -6 & \\le f(x)\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $f(x)\\in [-6,2].$",
